  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 132 AM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nA low (15-20%) chance of showers and thunderstorms are expected \ntoday, mainly the Coastal Bend and Victoria Crossroads. Less \nmoisture and mid level ridging across the Mexico and along the Rio \nGrande will limit convection today. The ridge is progged to shift \nfarther east Saturday leading to very low rain chances. Rain chances \nincrease Sunday in response to the ridge being nudged northward as \nan inverted trough shifts west across S TX. This will allow for \ndeeper moisture to interact with the sea breeze. The best chance \nwill be across the Victoria Crossroads where deeper moisture will \nreside. Isolated sea breeze convection is expected early next week \nwith the potential for increased activity by mid week. \n\nAn Extreme risk of heat related impacts are forecast across most of \nS TX today through the weekend. Heat indices up to 110-114 are \nexpected across a majority of S TX this afternoon lasting 4-6 hours.\nTherefore, a Heat Advisory has been issued for S TX from Noon to 7 \nPM. Heat Advisory conditions are expected again Saturday and \npossibly Sunday.",
